=== PARITY (web DoorWindowStatusWidget.tsx → SwiftUI) ===
  Registry (registry/security.ts):  id="door-window-status", category=security,
    defaultSize 2×2, minSize 1×2, maxSize 4×40, icon DoorOpen → SF Symbol
    "door.left.hand.open". Reproduced verbatim in DoorWindowStatusWidget.descriptor
    + DashboardWidgetDescriptor.clampedSize (size-constraint honoring, unit-tested).
  Data: /security/latest?vehicle_id= → SecurityEvent{door_state, fd/fp/rd/rp_window:
    string|bool|null}. Modeled by DoorWindowRawValue(.string/.bool/.absent).
  Adapter: parseDoorStates (bool→all; all_closed/allclosed; comma descriptors
    driver/passenger × front/rear × open, positional front/rear left/right open,
    bare "open"→all) + parseWindowState (bool; "closed"; vent/partial→partial;
    else open) + counts (doors strictly==open; windows !=closed && !=unknown) +
    toGridStatus (closed→ok, open/partial→warning, unknown). Ported verbatim.
  Composition: compact 1×1 = two summary badges; ≥2 rows = Doors grid(2) +
    Windows grid(2); isTall (rows≥2) widens spacing. All branches reproduced.
  States (all render, none hidden): loading skeleton; empty grid "No
    door/window data"; error → TSQueryError + retry; stale chip; offline →
    cached value kept + offline chip. Mapped onto LoadableState + FacadeError.
  Binding (P1/S8): view performs NO IO; DoorWindowStatusModel owns an injected
    DoorWindowStatusDataSource seam (production wires the shared state-holder/HTTP
    layer; previews/tests inject fixtures) — same injected-store pattern as
    VehicleSettingsModel / AppSettingsModel.
  i18n (P1/S10): all 15 widget.doorWindow.* keys already exist in the neutral
    catalog apps/shared/i18n/catalog/en.json (acceptance "matching key in P1/S10
    catalog" = MET). The generated Apple Localizable.xcstrings was stale for them;
    18 keys (15 + displayName + description + freshness.refresh) were added to the
    Apple resource with the canonical values, matching the existing native widget-
    key convention (e.g. widget.alerts.displayName). No hardcoded English in Swift.
  Telemetry (P1/S11): DashboardWidgetDiagnostics seam emits view.opened with
    surface slug "DoorWindowStatusWidget" once on first onAppear (forwardable to
    Telemetry.track(.ScreenView(...))). Unit-tested.

